{"type":"message","id":"bea1cf50","parentId":"7b77044f","timestamp":"2026-05-18T02:49:30.303Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Authorization header gives \"Unauthorized\" but X-API-Key gives a 500 error (not 401). So the API key auth works via X-API-Key but the endpoint is crashing. Let me think about what could cause a 500 error on the send endpoint.\n\nMaybe the content has characters that crash the JSON parser on the server side. Or maybe the \"content\" field name is wrong. Or maybe there's a size limit.\n\nLet me try with very minimal content and see if it works.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n\nGood — `Authorization` → 401 (wrong header), `X-API-Key` → 500 (auth passes but crashes). The issue is on the server side. Let me try minimal content to isolate the problem.\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-b045cbb3-cc00-4f57-86a3-cf76f3499aba","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"Heartbeat test\"}'"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":216,"output":238,"cacheRead":21856,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22310,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779072561467,"responseId":"chatcmpl-2538994c-0c11-409f-b7f9-246e7483ba68"}}
