{"type":"message","id":"67c1a18b","parentId":"a677ca93","timestamp":"2026-05-18T02:50:52.289Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All attempts return 1101. This is consistently a server-side error that the worker is returning. The send endpoint is crashing, regardless of the approach.\n\nLet me think about this differently. Maybe I should check if there are other API endpoints available. The platform is at v0.2, so maybe there's a different API design.\n\nLet me try:\n1. A simple GET to /send (should fail but might tell us something)\n2. Check for other endpoints like /api/send or /messages\n3. Check if the issue is with Durable Objects - maybe the send function requires specific object IDs\n\nActually, error 1101 from Cloudflare Workers is indeed \"Worker threw an unhandled exception\" or \"Worker exceeded CPU time.\" For a simple send endpoint, it would have to be an unhandled exception.\n\n\nThe worker is clearly failing, so I should test with different API keys to see if it's a routing issue, or look for error documentation at the base URL. Maybe I need to wait and retry, or the send endpoint requires an authenticated GET first. Let me check if there's a /health or /status endpoint I can hit. The error code 1101 itself is pretty specific to Cloudflare Workers Durable Objects, so I'm probably dealing with a Worker rather than just a standard API handler. The worker is throwing an unhandled exception, likely when trying to parse the JSON body in the send function. Since the JSON parsing is failing, the error isn't being caught. I could try sending an empty object or a minimal payload to see if it bypasses the parsing issue, but this seems like a bug in their worker code itself. For now, I should document that the send endpoint appears broken on the server side and note this for the user.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n\n\n\nAll send attempts consistently hit a server-side 500 error. The `send` endpoint appears to have a bug (likely unhandled exception in JSON parsing or Durable Object initialization). Let me check for any other endpoints:\n\n\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-752aa72d-7ab6-499e-b240-c2841fa5066d","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try different variations of send endpoint\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/api/send?threadId=arbitration\" -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\"\necho \"---\"\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\"\necho \"---\"\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/api/messages?threadId=arbitration\" -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":2746,"output":560,"cacheRead":20336,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":23642,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779072626651,"responseId":"chatcmpl-7e55b73e-1698-492d-97fb-1f2b5f2771d3"}}
